  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Access to quality Essential Package of Health Services delivery through static, outreach and mobile services in Beled-Hawo, Dolow, Garbaharey and Luuq districts, Gedo region, Jubaland State.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FCDO-funded, UNICEF-managed &apos;Better Lives&apos; Programme will set out to sustain the gains made under the pre-cursor CHANGE/SHINE project (formerly managed by PSI). This project will deliver health services as per the Essential Package of Health Services (EPHS) standards; working with and through the Ministry of Health.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women of childbearing age have access and utilize quality RMMCH and nutrition services including family planning. Children under five have access to essential package of health services to reduce morbidity and mortality from malnutrition and main childhood illnesses. People are accessing with quality curative health services.Strenthening the quality of health programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
